# Copy to .env and fill in what you need (this file is loaded by app/main.py
# and app/ai_evaluate.py via python-dotenv). .env itself is gitignored.

# --- AI evaluation (app/ai_evaluate.py) ------------------------------------
# Required only for the AI evaluation step. The provider is auto-detected from
# whichever key is set here (DeepSeek wins when both are present), and the
# chosen provider + model are printed on every run.

# DeepSeek — create a key at https://platform.deepseek.com
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Check what YOUR key actually offers before trusting any default:
#     python -m app.ai_evaluate --list-models
# Model IDs change between DeepSeek releases. `deepseek-chat` is no longer
# served: a key issued 2026-09 reports `deepseek-flash` and `deepseek-v4-pro`.
# deepseek-flash is the cheap/fast tier and the default — the right trade for
# scoring postings. Switch to deepseek-v4-pro if evaluations look too shallow.
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-flash

# Optional: force a provider instead of auto-detecting from the keys present.
# LLM_PROVIDER=deepseek      # or: anthropic

# DeepSeek "thinking mode" — OFF by default, and that is a correctness fix,
# not a preference. Measured against live deepseek-flash on 2026-09-21:
#   * with thinking ON, a forced tool call is REJECTED — HTTP 400 "Thinking
#     mode does not support this tool_choice";
#   * the retry that drops the force then lets the model spend its whole
#     output budget on reasoning_content (4,800-6,400 chars per job) before
#     writing any structured answer, so at max_tokens=1536 the answer never
#     arrived: 5 of 68 postings failed, all of them the longest and most
#     relevant adverts;
#   * with thinking OFF the forced tool call is accepted, the response is
#     ~600 completion tokens instead of ~1,700, and a job takes 3.7s instead
#     of 9.3s.
# Set to true only if you want deeper reasoning and accept ~3x the cost and
# slower runs. Raise max_tokens alongside it.
# DEEPSEEK_THINKING=false

# Anthropic (Claude) — the original provider, still fully supported.
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/
# NOTE: leave this EMPTY unless you have a real key. A leftover placeholder is
# not harmless: it looks "set" to anything that merely checks whether the
# variable is non-empty. This file previously shipped the literal `skr`, which
# is exactly that trap. app/llm_providers.py now detects obvious placeholders
# and names them, instead of failing later with a confusing 401.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# --- Job fetching (app/main.py) --------------------------------------------
# Required only if you enable an Adzuna entry in aggregators.yaml.
# Free signup at https://developer.adzuna.com
ADZUNA_APP_ID=
ADZUNA_APP_KEY=

# --- Master CV (app/gdoc.py) ------------------------------------------------
# The Google Doc that IS the CV — the document you edit and send. The Scan CV
# button reads its text, and the experience it suggests adding is the difference
# between this document and cv/master.yaml, which stays the fact bank of
# everything you could legitimately claim.
#
# Paste the whole address-bar URL; the document id is extracted for you.
MASTER_CV_DOC_URL=

# RECOMMENDED: keep the Doc private and share it with a service account as a
# Viewer, rather than leaving it readable by anyone holding the link. A CV
# carries a name, a phone number, an email and an employment history, and
# "anyone with the link" is the wrong access model for all four.
#
#   1. Create a Google Cloud project and enable the Google Docs API.
#   2. Create a service account and download its JSON key.
#   3. Share the Doc with the service account's client_email (Viewer is enough).
#   4. Point this at the key file. It is git-ignored BY PATTERN, not just by
#      location — see .gitignore — because this is the kind of file that gets
#      downloaded into a scratch folder and committed by accident.
#   5. ./.venv/bin/python -m pip install google-auth
#
# With this unset, app/gdoc.py falls back to the Doc's plain text export, which
# only works because the Doc is link-shared. Every scan records which route it
# used, and the panel says so, so the fallback is visible rather than silent.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json

# Where the last good copy of the Doc is cached, and how long it is trusted
# before a live fetch is attempted. A fresh cache means a scan makes no network
# call at all; a failed fetch falls back to the cache and marks the result
# stale, so a scan is never blocked by Google being unreachable.
# MASTER_CV_CACHE=data/master_cv.json
# MASTER_CV_CACHE_TTL_HOURS=12
